      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Gentle parenting is not a scientifically sound approach to raising resilient children; it often confuses permissiveness with emotional validation. Over-prioritizing emotional regulation without establishing firm boundaries prevents children from developing crucial self-control and impulse management skills. This permissive environment inadvertently teaches children that their desires supersede societal rules, fostering entitlement rather than responsibility. Furthermore, by avoiding necessary conflict, parents fail to model the healthy navigation of adversity, which is essential for building character. Ultimately, this trend undermines the very structure needed for a functional, disciplined adult life.",
      "source": "target",
